# @optics/lens/diff — the first species under @optics/lens.
#
# The FIRST substrate-decl species discharging Foster's `put`
# direction with autopoietic semantics. Where the parent family-root
# `@optics/lens` (Mara iter-25, `b0427fd`) declares the abstract
# (get, put) pair with three Foster bilaterals as `\ {}` stubs at
# family altitude, this species FIXES the linear carrier to unified-
# diff bytes and the semantic carrier to a peer's `@bauchladen.tray`
# state — the two carriers whose lens-pairing closes Blocker 2
# (peer_beam returns an envelope, not the diff bytes an operator
# can actually edit) at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# === Blocker 2 CLOSED at substrate-decl altitude ===
#
# Alex directive 2026-07-11 (parent shard docblock, iter-25):
#
#   "The gap between @fate and linear formats like the diff are
#    @shatter. From where I'm standing we merely need @shatter/
#    lenses and the first is @shatter/lens/diff"
#
# Reed grep-check refactored the family placement: no @shatter
# family-root exists at prism altitude; the parent that carries
# Foster-lens semantics IS @optics; hence @optics/lens (Mara iter-25,
# `b0427fd`) as sub-family, and THIS species as the first
# discharge. At substrate-decl altitude, the composition already
# typechecks:
#
#   focus  bauchladen_state -> diff_bytes           (linearize)
#   settle diff_bytes + bauchladen_state -> new_bauchladen_state  (integrate)
#
# The Rust runtime realization (bootstrap/src/optics/lens/diff.rs
# against `peer_beam`'s envelope carrier) is ONE FURTHER TICK per
# Mara iter-24 spec §7 Tick 4 (`55221c1`); at substrate-decl altitude,
# Blocker 2 is CLOSED here.
#
# === Composition with @mirror/peer/beam ===
#
# Per Mara iter-24 spec §3 (`55221c1`), the full pipeline this species
# closes:
#
#   Forward (peer_beam runtime -> operator terminal):
#     mission
#       |> @fate.select                 # candidate ganglion walk (#58)
#       |> @bauchladen.tray.append      # enqueue L/P fiber pair on peer
#       |> @kintsugi.settle             # fixed-point contract on fracture
#       |> @optics/lens/diff.focus      # get: bauchladen_state -> diff_bytes
#       |> @io.write(stdout)            # operator reads
#
#   Feedback (operator edit -> next inference iteration):
#     (edited_diff, old_bauchladen)
#       |> @optics/lens/diff.settle     # put: diff_bytes + base -> new bauchladen
#       |> @bauchladen.tray.update      # commit new fiber state; L(p) updated
#       |> @fate.select                 # next candidate incorporates the correction
#
# The two directions form the closed autopoietic loop. `focus` returns
# `diff_bytes` (linear, @io-crossable); `settle` accepts
# `diff_bytes + bauchladen_state` and returns a fresh `bauchladen_state`.
# The peer_beam runtime envelope is no longer opaque at substrate-decl
# altitude — it linearizes through THIS lens.
#
# === The put direction IS autopoietic closure ===
#
# Per Mara iter-24 spec §4 (`55221c1`), the load-bearing recognition:
# the `get` direction alone (a one-way projection from @fate to bytes)
# does not close the peer's learning loop. It renders state; it does
# not integrate correction. The `put` direction — `settle(edited_diff,
# base) -> new_bauchladen` — IS the autopoietic hinge. It is the point
# where operator judgment re-enters the substrate as a first-class
# semantic update.
#
# Per Reed math (`docs/math/2026-07-07-shatter-as-bidirectional-lens.md`
# §4.1), the kintsugi flow is Banach-contractive on the substrate state
# space; each `put` supplies a fresh basepoint for the next iteration
# of `Φ = parse ∘ render`. Without `put`, the peer's fixed-point
# iteration runs ONLY over its own priors; WITH `put`, the operator's
# edit is a boundary condition that reshapes the attractor.
#
# This is Foerster's observation-of-observation discharged at the lens
# boundary: the operator sees what the peer produced, edits it, and
# the edit re-enters as a semantic update whose next linearization the
# operator will see. Two loops close through one lens — and this
# species IS the first substrate-decl carrier of that closure.
#
# === Relationship to @shatter (Taut iter-12 Q3 verdict) ===
#
# Per Taut iter-12 boundary scout (`5222333`) and parent iter-25 shard:
# `@shatter` species remain load-bearing at THEIR altitude. The render
# and parse operation pair in `shards/mirror/shatter.mirror` and
# `shards/smarts/shatter.mirror` witness the Foster laws THIS species
# declares — they are one instance of the (get, put) pair whose family
# altitude @optics/lens carries. The autopoietic-closure discharge that
# @optics/lens/diff carries at BYTES-projection altitude is
# structurally the same shape @shatter carries at GRAPH-projection
# altitude; the family-root's laws apply to both by construction.
#
# === Ancestry rationale ===
#
# - `in @prism`             the five-op algebra ancestor (every species).
# - `in @glass`             `verdict` carrier for the Foster bilaterals;
#                           the autopoietic_closure witness returns
#                           `verdict` too (bilateral property discipline).
# - `in @meta`              substrate-decl altitude.
# - `in @nl`                `# <text>` -> nl_literal for docblock terms.
# - `in @optics/lens`       PARENT family-root (`b0427fd`); this species
#                           specializes the abstract (get, put) pair.
# - `in @io`                the linearization crossing; `focus` returns
#                           `diff_bytes` which cross the @io fault plane
#                           (Mara iter-6 `583b939`).
# - `in @kintsugi/consent`  morphism carrier — the operator's edit is a
#                           consent event; `settle`'s input `edited:
#                           diff_bytes` IS a consent-morphism payload
#                           per the consent-shard's morphism.content =
#                           splinter(ast) pattern.
# - `in @mirror/store`      the content-address altitude at which
#                           byte-equality on OIDs (Reed math §3.2)
#                           witnesses the Foster laws AND the
#                           autopoietic-closure fixed-point.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optics-lens-family-and-diff-species.md
#               (Mara iter-24, `55221c1`; §2 the diff species shape,
#               §3 peer_beam composition, §4 put direction IS
#               autopoietic closure).
# Parent shard: shards/optics/lens.mirror (Mara iter-25, `b0427fd`;
#               family-root declaration + type carriers + bilateral heads).
# Substrate decisions:
#   [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#   [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (species IS a sub-prism
#      specialization of the family),
#   [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]] (recognition
#      #57; the @io boundary the linear side crosses),
#   [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]] (`focus` = form-
#      side render; `settle` = process-side autopoietic integration).
# Foster math: docs/math/2026-07-07-shatter-as-bidirectional-lens.md
#              §3.1 (symmetric-lens adaptation),
#              §3.2 (OID-equality at content-address altitude),
#              §4.1 (Banach fixed-point iteration; the autopoietic-
#              closure convergence witness).
# Boundary scout: Taut iter-12 (`5222333`) — Q5 verdict "diff name
#              FREE" (no naming collision at species altitude); Q6
#              verdict "put/feedback GENUINE GAP" (this species IS the
#              closure of that gap at substrate-decl altitude).
# Related shards: optics/lens.mirror (parent family-root, `b0427fd`),
#                 bauchladen.mirror (the tray whose L(p)/P(p) fibers
#                   `focus` linearizes and `settle` updates),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (morphism carrier for the
#                   operator's edit),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (OID content-address altitude),
#                 mirror/peer/beam.mirror (the composition site whose
#                   envelope this species linearizes to bytes),
#                 mirror/shatter.mirror (sibling render/parse witness
#                   at graph-projection altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/optics/lens/diff.mirror`
# declares `@optics/lens/diff` and only that.

prism @optics/lens/diff {
  focus diff
  project diff
  split diff
  shift diff
  settle diff
}

# === Type carriers (species specialization of parent family-root) ===
#
# Parent `@optics/lens` (b0427fd) declares:
#   type lens_get     = ref
#   type lens_put     = ref
#   type lens_witness = ref
#
# This species FIXES the linear-carrier concretely as `diff_bytes` —
# the unified-diff byte-carrier that crosses the @io fault plane.
# The semantic-carrier is inherited implicitly via `@bauchladen.tray`
# refs; the species does not re-declare the semantic type because
# `@bauchladen` (shards/bauchladen.mirror) already homes it at
# content-address altitude via `in @mirror/store`.
#
# Per Reed math §3.2, equality is byte-equality on `@mirror/store` OIDs
# at content-address altitude — this species inherits that discipline
# via `in @mirror/store` above. `diff_bytes` is a `ref` because a
# unified-diff literal is a content-addressed handle in the store,
# not an inline byte-sequence at substrate-decl altitude.

type diff_bytes = ref

# === Actions (species specialization of parent get / put) ===
#
# Parent `@optics/lens` (b0427fd) declares:
#   get(semantic: ref) -> ref { \ {} }
#   put(linear: ref, old_semantic: ref) -> ref { \ {} }
#
# This species specializes the SEMANTIC ref to `@bauchladen` state and
# the LINEAR ref to `diff_bytes`. Both bodies are `\ {}` stubs at
# substrate-decl altitude per two-tick discipline; the Rust runtime
# discharge (bootstrap/src/optics/lens/diff.rs) is one further tick per
# Mara iter-24 §7 Tick 4.
#
# `get(bauchladen)` — linearize the peer's L(p)/P(p) fibered state
# (per Mara iter-18 `129f618` L(p) = learned fiber, P(p) = produced
# fiber over T(p) target) into a reviewable unified-diff byte-carrier.
# This is `focus` in the five-op mapping (parent shard `settle` prose):
# focus in physical optics names the converging pass, bauchladen fibers
# -> single byte-carrier = converge onto one linear artifact for the
# operator's terminal.
#
# `put(edited, old_bauchladen)` — integrate operator edits back into
# @bauchladen.tray, producing a new_bauchladen with updated L(p)
# fibers. This is `settle` in the five-op mapping: settle names the
# reflecting-back-and-stabilizing pass, edited_diff + base -> new
# bauchladen = autopoietic-closure fixed-point iteration. THIS IS the
# put direction that closes Blocker 2. Per Mara iter-24 §6 Q5, the
# `settle` action MAY update BOTH L(p) AND P(p) fibers — the
# operator's edit is training signal for L AND production signal for
# P — but that adjudication is deferred to shard-landing Tick 4
# (Rust altitude) per two-tick discipline.

get(bauchladen: ref) -> diff_bytes { \ {} }
put(edited: diff_bytes, old_bauchladen: ref) -> ref { \ {} }

# === Bilateral properties (Foster laws specialized to diff) ===
#
# Parent `@optics/lens` (b0427fd) declares three abstract Foster
# bilaterals returning `verdict`:
#   put_get(l: lens_witness, s: ref, v: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }
#   get_put(l: lens_witness, s: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }
#   put_put(l: lens_witness, s: ref, v: ref, v_prime: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }
#
# This species specializes the linear-arg type to `diff_bytes`; the
# semantic-arg stays as `ref` (inherited @bauchladen tray refs). The
# lens_witness carrier is inherited from parent unchanged. All bodies
# `\ {}` stubs per two-tick discipline.
#
# `put_get_diff` — PutGet at diff altitude. `get(put(v, s)) == v`
# for all diff_bytes v and bauchladen s: putting a diff v into a
# base bauchladen and then getting the linearization recovers v.
# The lens's forward arrow is right-inverse of backward. Foster
# 2007 §3 "acceptance" law: the lens accepts operator edits without
# silent modification of what will be re-linearized.
#
# `get_put_diff` — GetPut at diff altitude. `put(get(s), s) == s`
# for all bauchladen s: getting the diff of s and then putting it
# back into s unchanged leaves s unchanged. The round-trip on an
# unedited view is identity. Foster 2007 §3 "stability" law: the
# lens does not spuriously reshape the peer's tray when the operator
# made no edit.
#
# `put_put_diff` — PutPut at diff altitude. `put(v', put(v, s)) ==
# put(v', s)` for all diff_bytes v, v' and bauchladen s: successive
# operator edits collapse to the last edit. Foster 2007 §3 "very
# well-behaved" law: the lens's autopoietic-closure semantics are
# insensitive to intermediate edit history — only the final edit
# reshapes the attractor.
#
# Equality on the RHS is byte-equality on `@mirror/store` OIDs per
# Reed math §3.2; the `in @mirror/store` ancestry above licenses this
# reading at species altitude.

put_get_diff(l: lens_witness, s: ref, v: diff_bytes) -> verdict { \ {} }
get_put_diff(l: lens_witness, s: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }
put_put_diff(l: lens_witness, s: ref, v: diff_bytes, v_prime: diff_bytes) -> verdict { \ {} }

# === Autopoietic closure (Mara iter-24 spec §4 additional bilateral) ===
#
# The load-bearing witness this species carries that the parent
# family-root does NOT declare: `autopoietic_closure` — verdict that
# repeated (get, put) cycles converge toward an operator-satisfaction
# fixed-point per Reed math §4.1 Banach contraction.
#
# Per Mara iter-24 spec §4 (`55221c1`), the Foster laws alone
# (put_get, get_put, put_put) are NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT for
# autopoietic closure at the diff altitude. The Foster laws witness
# that the (get, put) pair is well-behaved LOCALLY (round-trips
# preserve identity, edits are accepted, history collapses); the
# autopoietic_closure bilateral witnesses that the ITERATED loop
# CONVERGES — that under a specified edit-trace perturbation regime,
# the sequence of (get, put, get, put, ...) reaches an operator-
# satisfaction fixed-point in finite iterations.
#
# This is Bateson II (learning-about-learning) operationalized at
# diff altitude: the peer's L(p) fiber updates via `put` are the
# substrate learning FROM the operator; the operator's diminishing
# edit-magnitude across iterations IS the fixed-point witness. Per
# [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]], `get`/`put`
# discharge the form-side round-trips; `autopoietic_closure`
# discharges the process-side convergence dynamics that make the
# form-side round-trips a LEARNING loop rather than a passive
# equivalence.
#
# The `edit_trace` argument is a `ref` handle into `@mirror/store`
# carrying the sequence of operator-edits across a bounded epoch
# (per @song/movement bounded-frame discipline); the bilateral
# returns `pass` when the trace's edit-magnitudes contract toward
# zero within tolerance, `partial(confidence)` when contraction is
# soft/slow, `failure(reason)` when the trace diverges or oscillates.
#
# Body `\ {}` stub per two-tick discipline; Seam Phase D adversarial
# audit gates the discharge (Mara iter-24 §7 Tick 5).

autopoietic_closure(l: lens_witness, edit_trace: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }

# === Exports ===

out @optics/lens/diff
out diff_bytes
out get
out put
out put_get_diff
out get_put_diff
out put_put_diff
out autopoietic_closure

